  "notes": [
    "Source is the Epson SG3225EEN / VEN product brief (2 pages, (c) Seiko Epson 2025); the full datasheet is available from Epson on request. All values are read from the LV-PECL (SG3225EEN) column.",
    "frequency_tolerance is a single all-inclusive figure (initial tolerance + temperature + supply-voltage change + long-term aging at +25 C). The brief's merged remark cells associate 5-year aging with the +/-25 ppm (D) grade and 10-year aging with the +/-50 / +/-100 ppm (J / L) grades; this document uses the J grade (+/-50 ppm).",
    "LV-PECL VOH (VCC - 1.1 V min) and VOL (VCC - 1.5 V max) are computed to absolute volts at the ordered VCC = 3.3 V; the printed VCC-relative form is kept in conditionsVerbatim.",
    "The phase-jitter measurements are the printed SG3225EEN product-family characterization curve across carrier frequencies (100 / 125 / 156.25 / 200 / 312.5 / 491.52 MHz, integration band 12 kHz to 20 MHz). The ordered part outputs 156.25 MHz, whose guaranteed headline is 50 fs typ.",
    "Ordered grade for this document: SG3225EEN 156.250000M-CJGA = C (3.3 V) / J (+/-50 ppm) / G (-40 to +85 C) / A (default internal code), product number X1G005221xxxx00."
